1
00:00:00,437 --> 00:00:02,343
You are in the decision meeting.

2
00:00:02,395 --> 00:00:06,757
Before opening the scorecard, read the
rules the team approved at kickoff.

3
00:00:06,861 --> 00:00:09,405
Expand when the benefit and guardrails
are met.

4
00:00:10,034 --> 00:00:14,238
Adjust when a specific issue can be
addressed in a bounded follow-up.

5
00:00:14,317 --> 00:00:17,503
Pause for a serious data or access
incident,

6
00:00:17,581 --> 00:00:20,967
or when the quality risk needs
investigation before continuing.

7
00:00:21,607 --> 00:00:26,125
This sequence matters because a strong
speed result is easy to focus on.

8
00:00:26,177 --> 00:00:28,632
Put all three decisions on the table.

9
00:00:28,710 --> 00:00:32,575
Ask a teammate which evidence would make
them choose each one before showing the

10
00:00:32,628 --> 00:00:33,521
pilot numbers.

11
00:00:35,724 --> 00:00:37,422
Walk down the scorecard.

12
00:00:37,500 --> 00:00:40,608
Wait is thirteen business hours against
fourteen.

13
00:00:40,686 --> 00:00:43,738
Active review is twenty-six minutes
against twenty-seven.

14
00:00:44,416 --> 00:00:48,046
Spending is two hundred and forty
dollars against three hundred.

15
00:00:48,124 --> 00:00:50,057
Each clears its threshold.

16
00:00:50,161 --> 00:00:54,549
Seven of forty requests needed rework,
so that row lands at seventeen and a

17
00:00:54,601 --> 00:00:55,367
half percent.

18
00:00:55,997 --> 00:00:57,643
The ceiling was fifteen.

19
00:00:57,695 --> 00:01:02,030
The defect count is one in each group,
and there were zero serious data or

20
00:01:02,082 --> 00:01:03,675
access incidents.

21
00:01:03,754 --> 00:01:06,907
The rework row rules out expansion under
the team's agreement.

22
00:01:07,593 --> 00:01:10,391
Now check whether it gives you a clear
change to try.

23
00:01:12,259 --> 00:01:13,983
Pull up the review notes.

24
00:01:14,061 --> 00:01:18,997
Four of the seven rework cases included
files outside the intended change.

25
00:01:19,076 --> 00:01:23,085
In one of those cases the reviewer asked
to drop unrelated formatting.

26
00:01:23,724 --> 00:01:26,910
Turn that observation into two concrete
steps.

27
00:01:26,962 --> 00:01:31,794
The author lists the expected files in
Copilot Plan and checks every actual

28
00:01:31,846 --> 00:01:34,167
changed path before publishing the
branch.

29
00:01:34,840 --> 00:01:39,227
If a third file appears, the author asks
what it contributes to the stated

30
00:01:39,280 --> 00:01:41,238
acceptance criteria.

31
00:01:41,290 --> 00:01:44,681
The independent reviewer still checks
the final pull request.

32
00:01:45,366 --> 00:01:48,521
This is an adjustment the team can
observe in the follow-up.

33
00:01:50,453 --> 00:01:53,534
The engineering lead owns the next four
weeks.

34
00:01:53,613 --> 00:01:58,125
Keep the service, eligibility, and
metric definitions in place so the next

35
00:01:58,177 --> 00:02:00,143
readout can be compared with the pilot.

36
00:02:00,799 --> 00:02:05,344
At forty requests, six rework cases
would meet fifteen percent.

37
00:02:05,422 --> 00:02:10,044
If only thirty requests qualify, four
cases equal about thirteen point three

38
00:02:10,097 --> 00:02:13,378
percent and five equal about sixteen
point seven.

39
00:02:14,043 --> 00:02:16,159
Use the actual denominator.

40
00:02:16,237 --> 00:02:19,136
Check the reason each time work comes
back.

41
00:02:19,214 --> 00:02:22,478
You need evidence that the extra-file
pattern improved,

42
00:02:22,531 --> 00:02:25,926
together with the time and spending
measures that supported the original

43
00:02:25,978 --> 00:02:26,533
pilot.

44
00:02:28,744 --> 00:02:30,911
Try three short scenarios.

45
00:02:30,989 --> 00:02:35,951
First, the follow-up meets the wait,
effort, rework, and budget thresholds.

46
00:02:36,004 --> 00:02:39,916
Propose expansion to one comparable team
and name its onboarding owner.

47
00:02:40,615 --> 00:02:45,456
Second, one routine guardrail misses by
a little and review evidence points to a

48
00:02:45,535 --> 00:02:47,102
fixable cause.

49
00:02:47,180 --> 00:02:49,199
Consider another bounded adjustment.

50
00:02:49,851 --> 00:02:54,578
Third, someone sends restricted data to
an unapproved model endpoint.

51
00:02:54,656 --> 00:02:58,735
Pause the affected workflow and use the
existing incident process.

52
00:02:59,348 --> 00:03:03,187
Practice saying each decision with the
evidence that triggered it.

53
00:03:03,239 --> 00:03:06,764
The person who owns the next action
should hear exactly what to do.

54
00:03:08,997 --> 00:03:12,815
Open a decision record and fill in a
date, an owner, the decision,

55
00:03:12,867 --> 00:03:14,408
and the next review.

56
00:03:14,460 --> 00:03:16,654
For this case we choose adjust.

57
00:03:16,732 --> 00:03:19,772
Median wait met the target, rework did
not,

58
00:03:19,824 --> 00:03:22,895
and the extra-file pattern gives us a
focused intervention.

59
00:03:23,573 --> 00:03:27,961
Name the engineering lead, attach the
scorecard and the review evidence,

60
00:03:28,013 --> 00:03:31,114
and put a follow-up on the calendar four
weeks from the relaunch.

61
00:03:31,777 --> 00:03:33,814
Then hand the note to a teammate.

62
00:03:33,892 --> 00:03:37,574
If they can tell which workflow to
change and what evidence will determine

63
00:03:37,600 --> 00:03:40,035
the next decision, the record is ready.
